cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Anchor Audit Toolkit, cite this software and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Anchor Audit Toolkit"
version: 0.2.5
authors:
  - family-names: Iben
    given-names: Patrick
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2443-7973"
repository-code: "https://github.com/patrickiben/contact-map-anchor-audit"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit and interactive browser lab for auditing how a declared
  translation of finite persistence diagrams changes bottleneck distances,
  ties, and tolerance-aware rankings. Includes synthetic controls, endpoint
  bounds, witness-based partial rankings, and source-linked educational
  materials. Numerical checks do not constitute formal real-arithmetic,
  biological, or clinical validation.
keywords:
  - persistent homology
  - bottleneck distance
  - preprocessing audit
  - ranking stability
  - computational genomics
